## Hints

- E1: `np.linalg.solve(A, b)` solves Ax = b. Your A is (XᵀX), your b
  is (Xᵀy). Recover = |β̂ − 1.2| within ~2 SE of β̂; here SE(β̂) ≈
  σ_e/(σ_m√n) — compute it and compare the error to it.
- E2: `sm.OLS(y, sm.add_constant(x)).fit().params` returns [const, x].
- E4a: with no intercept, b = Σxy/Σx². If E[y] ≠ 0, the mean of y
  leaks into b. E4b: levels of integrated series correlate spuriously;
  check the residual ACF, not just R².
- E5: think along (i) sampling error, (ii) which time window, (iii)
  what the regressor leaves out.
